IMPORT prelude

-- Central Provident Fund Act 1953 (Singapore) -- what goes into my CPF each month from my job, what my employer may take from my
-- pay for it, and when my employer is exempt.
--
-- SEAT: the employee (the member of the Fund whose wages the contributions are paid on).
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 7(1) (the contribution duty), s 7(2) (what may be recovered from my wages), s 7(3) (keeping what was
-- deducted), s 7(5) (deducting too much), s 7(6) and (6A) (deducting only from the wages concerned, and catching up a missed
-- deduction); First Schedule paragraph 1 (the rates from 1 January 2026) and paragraph 5(a), (b), (c) and (ea) (when an older band
-- starts, rounding, the Ordinary Wage Ceiling); s 13(4) (crediting to my accounts, with the Minister's ratios as facts I state);
-- and the Central Provident Fund (Exemption) Order 2018, paragraphs 2 to 5 and the Schedule.
--
-- Edition: the Act in the 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 1 July 2026, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/CPFA1953.txt (First Schedule paragraph 1 as amended by S 886/2025 wef 1 January 2026); the
-- Exemption Order (S 61/2018) in the 2025 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 1 June 2026, as deposited
-- at ../../registers/source-bundle/CPFA1953-OR10.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED (each answers NOTHING where it would be needed): additional wages and the Relevant Additional Wages; the graduated
-- rates for a permanent resident up to the end of the second anniversary month (paragraphs 1A to 1D); the employees of the bodies in
-- paragraph 6 and the public-sector employees of paragraph 7; months before January 2026. Also out: s 7(1A), s 7(4) (voluntary
-- extra contributions, beyond what s 7(5) allows), s 7(7) (wages paid more often than monthly), s 7(8) and the rest of Part 3;
-- platform workers (s 8A and the Fourth Schedule); the 29 February rule in paragraph 5(a)(ii); and the machinery.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the employee, with the design defaults ruled on
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. It is not for public use as advice. See
-- NOTES.md.

§ `Central Provident Fund Act 1953 -- contributions on my wages, from the employee's seat`

§§ `The facts of my month`

DECLARE `Residence status` IS ONE OF
    `a citizen of Singapore`
    `a permanent resident past my second anniversary month`
    -- First Schedule para 5(ec): "second anniversary month" is the calendar month in which the second anniversary of the day I
    -- became a permanent resident falls. Until its end, paragraphs 1A to 1D set graduated rates, which are not encoded.
    `a permanent resident up to the end of my second anniversary month`
    `neither a citizen nor a permanent resident`

-- Exemption Order, the Schedule ("SPECIFIED EMPLOYEES"), as in force from 1 June 2026. Paragraphs 1, 4 and 5 are "[Deleted by
-- S 325/2026 wef 01/06/2026]". Whether an institution is on the list, or training was approved by it, is a fact I state.
DECLARE `Schedule class` IS ONE OF
    `none of the Schedule classes`
    -- para 2: "An employee of the United Nations Organisation, or any agency, institution or related organisation of the United
    -- Nations Organisation that is located in Singapore."
    `an employee of the United Nations or a related organisation in Singapore`
    -- para 2A: ICSID or MIGA (World Bank Group) located in Singapore.
    `an employee of ICSID or MIGA in Singapore`
    -- para 3: OECD employee assigned to the International Energy Agency Regional Cooperation Centre in Singapore.
    `an OECD employee at the IEA Regional Cooperation Centre in Singapore`
    -- para 6: "a matriculated or registered student of any of the following institutions and employed for training approved by
    -- the institution concerned: (a) any university whose function of providing university education is determined by any
    -- written law; (b) the Institute of Technical Education ...; (c) a polytechnic established by any written law; (d) a school
    -- specified in Part II or III of the Schedule to the ... (Edusave Pupils Fund) Regulations ...; (e) Mountbatten Vocational
    -- School."
    `a student of a listed institution employed for training it approved`
    -- para 7: a student of a private education institution, on a full-time programme subsidised by MOE and listed on its website,
    -- "employed for training approved by the private education institution".
    `a private education student on an MOE-subsidised full-time programme employed for training the institution approved`
    -- para 8: an overseas tertiary student required to train in Singapore "for a period of not more than 6 months", who gives the
    -- employer the institution's written confirmation.
    `an overseas tertiary student training here for not more than 6 months who gave my employer the written confirmation`
    -- para 9: a registered school student "(other than a student who has completed the GCE 'A' Level Examination or its
    -- equivalent)" of a listed school, "employed during a school holiday period".
    `a school student who has not completed A levels employed in a school holiday period`

-- One case is one month of wages from one employment.
DECLARE `My month of work` HAS
    `my residence status`                                                 IS A `Residence status`
    `my age in completed years`                                           IS A NUMBER
    -- First Schedule para 5(a)(i): an older band starts "from the first day of the month following the month in which the
    -- employee attains that age".
    `my birthday falls in this month`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the year`                                                            IS A NUMBER
    `the month`                                                           IS A NUMBER
    -- para 5(e): "ordinary wages for the month" is remuneration due "wholly or exclusively in respect of employment during that
    -- month and payable before the due date for the payment of contribution for that month".
    `my ordinary wages for the month`                                     IS A NUMBER
    `I have additional wages this month`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `my employer is a body in First Schedule paragraph 6, or I am a public-sector employee under paragraph 7` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my Schedule class`                                                   IS A `Schedule class`
    -- Exemption Order para 4(4): a "domestic employee" is employed by an individual exclusively in that individual's private
    -- domestic household and not in connection with a trade, business or profession carried on there.
    `I am a domestic employee`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    -- para 4(2)(b) and (c): my current contract, or a "prior connected contract", was entered into before 1 June 2026, and my
    -- employment under it started before 1 June 2026 and met the hours test up to 31 May 2026. The hours test in (c)(ii)(B) reads
    -- "in every period of 7 consecutive days falling within any one calendar month", which may mean some one month or each month:
    -- a fork the encoding does not choose, so this is a fact I state in the Order's words.
    `paragraph 4(2) of the Order is met for my domestic contract`         IS A BOOLEAN
    -- para 4(1): "in every period of 7 consecutive days falling within that month, X's domestic employment by Y under the current
    -- contract does not exceed 14 hours".
    `my domestic work did not exceed 14 hours in any 7 consecutive days of this month` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- para 5(2): I am a citizen seaman on Swedish, Norwegian or East Asiatic Co. terms, and my current contract or a prior
    -- connected contract was entered into before 1 June 2026, with employment under it started before then.
    `paragraph 5 of the Order covers me as a seaman`                      IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Exemption Order paragraphs 2 to 5 -- is my employer exempt`

-- Order para 2(1) and (2): an employer whose employee is specified in the Schedule "is exempt from paying ... (a) any contribution
-- to the Fund under section 7 of the Act".
-- Order para 3: "An employer is exempt from paying any contribution to the Fund under section 7 of the Act in respect of wages
-- payable to an employee who is not a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore."
-- Order para 4(1): the domestic employee's employer is exempt "for any month after 31 May 2026" if the hours test is met that month.
-- Order para 5(1): the seaman's employer is exempt "for any period after 31 May 2026".
GIVEN `my month` IS A `My month of work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this month after 31 May 2026` IF
        `my month`'s `the year` GREATER THAN 2026
    OR  (`my month`'s `the year` EQUALS 2026 AND `my month`'s `the month` AT LEAST 6)

GIVEN `my month` IS A `My month of work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a specified employee in the Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `my month`'s `my Schedule class`
    WHEN `none of the Schedule classes` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `my month` IS A `My month of work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I neither a citizen nor a permanent resident` IF
    CONSIDER `my month`'s `my residence status`
    WHEN `neither a citizen nor a permanent resident` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `my month` IS A `My month of work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employer exempt from paying CPF contributions for me this month` IF
        `Am I a specified employee in the Schedule` `my month`
    OR  `Am I neither a citizen nor a permanent resident` `my month`
    OR  (    `my month`'s `I am a domestic employee`
         AND `my month`'s `paragraph 4(2) of the Order is met for my domestic contract`
         AND `my month`'s `my domestic work did not exceed 14 hours in any 7 consecutive days of this month`
         AND `Is this month after 31 May 2026` `my month`)
    OR  (    `my month`'s `paragraph 5 of the Order covers me as a seaman`
         AND `Is this month after 31 May 2026` `my month`)

§§ `First Schedule paragraph 1 -- the rates from 1 January 2026`

-- Para 1: "Subject to paragraphs 1A to 7, with effect from 1 January 2026, the contributions payable by the employer and the amount
-- recoverable from the employee's wages are as follows". For each band (a) to (e):
--   wages "Exceeding $50 but not exceeding $500": the employer pays "17% of the Total Wages"; nothing is recoverable from me;
--   "Exceeding $500 but not exceeding $750": "17% of the Total Wages; and ... 0.6 of the difference between the Total Wages and
--   $500"; recoverable: "0.6 of the difference between the Total Wages and $500";
--   "Exceeding $750": "37% of the employee's ordinary wages for the month subject to a maximum of 37% of the Ordinary Wage Ceiling";
--   recoverable: "20% of the employee's ordinary wages for the month subject to a maximum of 20% of the Ordinary Wage Ceiling".
-- The tables are column-shifted in the .txt deposit; each band was read cell by cell.
DECLARE `Rate band` HAS
    `low rate`        IS A NUMBER   -- over $50 to $750: the employer's percentage of Total Wages
    `phase-in factor` IS A NUMBER   -- over $500 to $750: the factor on the excess over $500, all of it recoverable from me
    `total rate`      IS A NUMBER   -- over $750: the employer's total percentage of ordinary wages up to the ceiling
    `my rate`         IS A NUMBER   -- over $750: the part of it recoverable from my wages

-- Para 5(a): contributions for an employee "above 55, 60, 65 or 70 years of age are payable -- (i) from the first day of the month
-- following the month in which the employee attains that age". So the band for a month is set by the age I had attained before the
-- month began. READING (labelled): "that age" is the threshold itself (55, 60, 65 or 70), so the band "above 55" starts in the month
-- after my 55th birthday month, although band (a) is headed "55 years of age and below".
GIVEN `my month` IS A `My month of work`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What age had I attained before this month began` IS
    IF   `my month`'s `my birthday falls in this month`
    THEN `my month`'s `my age in completed years` MINUS 1
    ELSE `my month`'s `my age in completed years`

--                                                           low,   phase-in, total, mine
GIVEN `my month` IS A `My month of work`
GIVETH A `Rate band`
DECIDE `Which rate band am I in` IS
    BRANCH IF `age before the month` LESS THAN 55 THEN `Rate band` OF 0.17,  0.6,      0.37,  0.2
           IF `age before the month` LESS THAN 60 THEN `Rate band` OF 0.16,  0.54,     0.34,  0.18
           IF `age before the month` LESS THAN 65 THEN `Rate band` OF 0.125, 0.375,    0.25,  0.125
           IF `age before the month` LESS THAN 70 THEN `Rate band` OF 0.09,  0.225,    0.165, 0.075
           OTHERWISE                                   `Rate band` OF 0.075, 0.15,     0.125, 0.05
    WHERE
        `age before the month` MEANS `What age had I attained before this month began` `my month`

-- Para 5(ea): the "Ordinary Wage Ceiling" is $6,300 a month from September to December 2023, $6,800 in 2024, $7,400 in 2025, and
-- "in respect of each month in the year 2026 and every subsequent year, is $8,000".
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the Ordinary Wage Ceiling in` year IS
    BRANCH IF year AT LEAST 2026 THEN 8000
           IF year EQUALS   2025 THEN 7400
           IF year EQUALS   2024 THEN 6800
           OTHERWISE                  6300

-- Para 5(b): "the contribution payable by the employer is to be rounded off to the nearest dollar except, where the fraction of a
-- dollar is 50 cents, it is to be regarded as a dollar". Para 5(c): "in calculating the amount recoverable by the employer from the
-- employee's wages, a fraction of a dollar is to be ignored".
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `rounded to the nearest dollar, 50 cents up` x IS FLOOR (x PLUS 0.5)

GIVEN `my month` IS A `My month of work`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `my ordinary wages up to the ceiling` IS
    IF   w GREATER THAN `the Ordinary Wage Ceiling in` (`my month`'s `the year`)
    THEN `the Ordinary Wage Ceiling in` (`my month`'s `the year`)
    ELSE w
    WHERE w MEANS `my month`'s `my ordinary wages for the month`

GIVEN `my month` IS A `My month of work`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the total under paragraph 1 before rounding` IS
    BRANCH IF w AT MOST 50  THEN 0
           IF w AT MOST 500 THEN w TIMES b's `low rate`
           IF w AT MOST 750 THEN w TIMES b's `low rate` PLUS (w MINUS 500) TIMES b's `phase-in factor`
           OTHERWISE             `my ordinary wages up to the ceiling` `my month` TIMES b's `total rate`
    WHERE
        w MEANS `my month`'s `my ordinary wages for the month`
        b MEANS `Which rate band am I in` `my month`

GIVEN `my month` IS A `My month of work`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `my share under paragraph 1 before rounding` IS
    BRANCH IF w AT MOST 500 THEN 0
           IF w AT MOST 750 THEN (w MINUS 500) TIMES b's `phase-in factor`
           OTHERWISE             `my ordinary wages up to the ceiling` `my month` TIMES b's `my rate`
    WHERE
        w MEANS `my month`'s `my ordinary wages for the month`
        b MEANS `Which rate band am I in` `my month`

-- Where paragraph 1 does not reach my month, the encoding answers NOTHING rather than a figure it has no text for.
GIVEN `my month` IS A `My month of work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my month one this encoding cannot compute` IF
        `my month`'s `the year` LESS THAN 2026
    OR  `my month`'s `I have additional wages this month`
    OR  `my month`'s `my employer is a body in First Schedule paragraph 6, or I am a public-sector employee under paragraph 7`
    OR  CONSIDER `my month`'s `my residence status`
        WHEN `a permanent resident up to the end of my second anniversary month` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 7(1): "every employer of an employee must pay to the Fund monthly in respect of each employee contributions at the appropriate
-- rates set out in the First Schedule". The total paid into my CPF for the month.
GIVEN `my month` IS A `My month of work`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the total CPF contribution for my month` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `Is my employer exempt from paying CPF contributions for me this month` `my month` THEN JUST 0
        IF `Is my month one this encoding cannot compute` `my month` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST (`rounded to the nearest dollar, 50 cents up` (`the total under paragraph 1 before rounding` `my month`))

-- s 7(2): "Despite the provisions of any written law or any contract to the contrary, an employer is entitled to recover from the
-- monthly wages of an employee the amount shown in the First Schedule as so recoverable from the employee."
GIVEN `my month` IS A `My month of work`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most my employer may deduct from my wages for CPF this month` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `Is my employer exempt from paying CPF contributions for me this month` `my month` THEN JUST 0
        IF `Is my month one this encoding cannot compute` `my month` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST (FLOOR (`my share under paragraph 1 before rounding` `my month`))

-- What the employer bears itself: the total less what it may recover from me.
GIVEN `my month` IS A `My month of work`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much does my employer pay on top of my wages` IS
    CONSIDER `What is the total CPF contribution for my month` `my month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST total THEN
        CONSIDER `What is the most my employer may deduct from my wages for CPF this month` `my month`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST mine THEN JUST (total MINUS mine)

§§ `7(3), 7(5), 7(6) and 7(6A) -- what my employer may not do with my share`

-- s 7(3): "Where any employer who has recovered any amount from the monthly wages of an employee in accordance with subsection (2)
-- fails to pay the contributions to the Fund within such time as may be prescribed, the employer shall be guilty of an offence and
-- shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 7 years or to both."
-- It bites only where my share was already taken from my pay.
GIVEN `my employer deducted my share from my wages` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my employer paid the contributions to the Fund within the prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my employer committed an offence by keeping my deducted share` IF
        `my employer deducted my share from my wages`
    AND NOT `my employer paid the contributions to the Fund within the prescribed time`

`the longest prison term my employer faces under section 7(3), in years` MEANS 7
`the largest fine my employer faces under section 7(3)` MEANS 10000

-- s 7(5): "Despite any contract to the contrary, an employer is not entitled to recover in any way from an employee in respect of
-- contributions payable under this Act any sum in excess of that permitted to be recovered under subsection (2) together with any
-- sum contributed voluntarily by the employee under subsection (4) and any employer who recovers or attempts to recover any greater
-- sum shall be guilty of an offence." The penalty is s 61(2): a fine of not less than $1,000 and not more than $5,000, or up to
-- 6 months, or both.
GIVEN `the amount my employer took from me for CPF` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount the First Schedule lets it recover` IS A NUMBER
      `what I chose to contribute voluntarily under section 7(4)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my employer committed an offence by taking too much` IF
    `the amount my employer took from me for CPF`
        GREATER THAN `the amount the First Schedule lets it recover` PLUS `what I chose to contribute voluntarily under section 7(4)`

-- s 7(6): my share "shall be recovered by the employer from the wages in respect of which the contribution is payable at the time of
-- payment of those wages and not otherwise".
-- s 7(6A): "Subject to such conditions as the Board may prescribe, where an employer has, by error not occasioned by that employer's
-- negligence, omitted to recover from the wages paid to an employee any amount ..., the amount ... may be recovered from the wages
-- payable by the employer to the employee not later than 6 months from the date of the payment of the wages in respect of which the
-- amount ... was omitted to be recovered."
GIVEN `my employer missed the deduction by an error not caused by its negligence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the later wages are paid not later than 6 months after the wages it missed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Board's prescribed conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my employer take a missed CPF deduction from my later wages` IF
        `my employer missed the deduction by an error not caused by its negligence`
    AND `the later wages are paid not later than 6 months after the wages it missed`
    AND `the Board's prescribed conditions are met`

§§ `13(4) -- which of my accounts it goes to`

-- s 13(1): my accounts are "(a) an ordinary account; (b) a medisave account; (c) a special account or a retirement account, or both".
-- s 13(4): "The Board must credit to the accounts of a member ..., in such manner as the Minister may direct, every contribution paid
-- into the Fund for the member under -- (a) section 7; ... (b) section 9A".
-- The Minister's direction is not subsidiary legislation and is not deposited, so the ratios are facts I state (the CPF Board
-- publishes them). INFERENCE (labelled): the medisave and special or retirement credits are each rounded to the nearest cent and the
-- ordinary account takes the remainder; the Act says nothing of rounding here.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `to the nearest cent` x IS FLOOR (x TIMES 100 PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `the contribution` IS A NUMBER
      `the Minister's medisave ratio for me` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my contribution goes to my medisave account` IS
    `to the nearest cent` (`the contribution` TIMES `the Minister's medisave ratio for me`)

GIVEN `the contribution` IS A NUMBER
      `the Minister's medisave ratio for me` IS A NUMBER
      `the Minister's special or retirement account ratio for me` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my contribution goes to my ordinary account` IS
    `the contribution`
        MINUS `How much of my contribution goes to my medisave account` `the contribution` `the Minister's medisave ratio for me`
        MINUS `to the nearest cent` (`the contribution` TIMES `the Minister's special or retirement account ratio for me`)
